        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{1}^{\\frac{e}{4}}\\frac{1}{4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\log{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\frac{e}{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}\u20614$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{1}^{\\frac{e}{4}}\\frac{1}{4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int_{1}^{\\frac{e}{4}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}Abs(u))\\right)|_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{1} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}1-\\operatorname{ln}(\\operatorname{ln}4))\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}(0-\\operatorname{ln}(\\operatorname{ln}4))\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}(\\operatorname{ln}4)\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
